\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Positioning against federated LoRA and client-selection systems. \text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}{} = the property holds in the cited papers' own descriptions; $\times $ = absent or not reported. Delivery-aware means that a scheduling or adaptation decision conditions on per-round network delivery state (rate, deadline, delivery probability) rather than on training progress, device capability, or static profiling alone. Real payload means payload is accounted as transmitted bytes rather than a fixed or parameter-count proxy. Real training means model training is executed in the evaluation as reported.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rwcompare}{{1}{6}{}{}{}}
\citation{mahboob2024ntn,razmi2022ground}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces FedRAS round pipeline. Action Construction (AC) scores every client--rank pair with the delivery hazard \eqref  {eq:hazard} and the saturating capacity \eqref  {eq:cap}; the GridDP assignment (GDP) computes the client--rank assignment under the byte budget and the admission cap. Updates arriving within the deadline $\tau $ pass the on-time gate and are merged by Masked Aggregation (MA) while the shared factor $A$ stays frozen; observed outcomes update the link-state history. AC, GDP, and MA correspond to Algorithms~\ref {alg:ac}--\ref {alg:ma}; the overall round is Algorithm~\ref {alg:fedras}.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{7}{}{}{}}
